ning it on Blu-ray/DVD (rather than relying on streaming) is the most reliable way to guarantee you always have access to that specific, unaltered version—since physical media doesn't get "updated" the way a streaming license can. So yes, it's a real risk, and it *does* happen, but it's not some ticking time bomb under every movie you love. It tends to hit older, lower-profile titles more than beloved blockbusters, and there are growing pressures (fan expectations, preservation efforts, broader up-front licensing) working against it.
