g contracts that can change what specific version reaches you, especially decades later or on new platforms. That's uncomfortable, but it's less "everything is unstable" and more "the *art* is fixed, but the *legal permissions to share that art* are not." If it helps: think of the version you watched and loved as "real" and complete in your memory and experience of it—nothing retroactively erases that. What changes is only what future versions distributed forward will contain.
